<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian TCorp says new issue well-received.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian TCorp says new issue well-received.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>New South Wales Treasury Corp (TCorp) said on Wednesday the tender for its new benchmark 2008 bond on Tuesday had been well received, and it would continue consolidations until the new issue totalled A$500 million.</p>
<p>The tender, for the 8.0 percent bond maturing March 1, 2008, received bids totalling A$750 million for the A$300 million issue. A total of A$360 million was issued via the tender at a weighted average yield of 8.244 percent.</p>
<p>To build up the new benchmark issue, TCorp began the offer of consolidations out of 2001, 2004 or 2006 TCorp bonds into the new 2008 bond on Tuesday morning.</p>
</text>
